`sort_unstable`](slice::sort_unstable). The exception are partially sorted slices, which"},{"DocComment":" may be better served with `slice::sort`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Sorting types that only implement [`PartialOrd`] such as [`f32`] and [`f64`] require"},{"DocComment":" additional precautions. For example, `f32::NAN != f32::NAN`, which doesn't fulfill the"},{"DocComment":" reflexivity requirement of [`Ord`]. By using an alternative comparison function with"},{"DocComment":" `slice::sort_by` such as [`f32::total_cmp`] or [`f64::total_cmp`] that defines a [total"},{"DocComment":" order] users can sort slices containing floating-point values. Alternatively, if all values"},{"DocComment":" in the slice are guaranteed to be in a subset for which [`PartialOrd::partial_cmp`] forms a"},{"DocComment":" [total order], it's possible to sort the slice with `sort_by(|a, b|"},{"DocComment":" a.partial_cmp(b).unwrap())`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Current implementation"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The current implementation is based on [driftsort] by Orson Peters and Lukas Bergdoll, which"},{"DocComment":" combines the fast average case of quicksort with the fast worst case and partial run"},{"DocComment":" detection of mergesort, achieving linear time on fully sorted and reversed inputs. On inputs"},{"DocComment":" with k distinct elements, the expected time to sort the data is *O*(*n* \\* log(*k*))."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The auxiliary memory allocation behavior depends on the input length. Short slices are"},{"DocComment":" handled without allocation, medium sized slices allocate `self.len()` and beyond that it"},{"DocComment":" clamps at `self.len() / 2`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" May panic if the implementation of [`Ord`] for `T` does not implement a [total order], or if"},{"DocComment":" the [`Ord`] implementation itself panics."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" All safe functions on slices preserve the invariant that even if the function panics, all"},{"DocComment":" original elements will remain in the slice and any possible modifications via interior"},{"DocComment":" mutability are observed in the input. This ensures that recovery code (for instance inside"},{"DocComment":" of a `Drop` or following a `catch_unwind`) will still have access to all the original"},{"DocComment":" elements. For instance, if the slice belongs to a `Vec`, the `Vec::drop` method will be able"},{"DocComment":" to dispose of all contained elements."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let mut v = [4, -5, 1, -3, 2];"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" v.sort();"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(v, [-5, -3, 1, 2, 4]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [driftsort]: https://github.com/Voultapher/driftsort"},{"DocComment":" [total order]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Total_order"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null,"diagnostic_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[{"index":0,"name":null,"variance":"Covariant","mutability":"Unknown"}],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T","variance":"Unknown"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"Deduplicated":0},"origin":"WhereClauseOnImpl","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":0}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":1,"span":{"Value":[23,{"data":{"file_id":7,"beg":{"line":133,"col":11},"end":{"line":133,"col":14}},"generated_from_span":null}]},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":4,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":0}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[{"regions":[],"skip_binder":[{"Deduplicated":0},{"Var":{"Bound":[1,0]}}]}],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust